# Keep the deploy payload to what actually builds the site.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working tree, which here is ~240 MB: 125 MB of
# workspace node_modules plus 59 MB of tracked snapshot goldens. That upload
# aborts. Git-triggered deploys clone instead and are the normal path, but a
# CLI deploy has to stay viable for one-off production pushes.
#
# Workspace package.json files must survive — `bun install --frozen-lockfile`
# resolves the root bun.lock against every workspace in package.json
# ("registry", "gallery", "www") and fails if one is missing. So this excludes
# gallery's *contents*, never the workspace manifest.

node_modules
.git

# 59 MB of PNG goldens for the snapshot gate. CI runs the gate; the deploy
# only builds the site, and never reads these.
gallery/harness/golden
gallery/harness/.candidate
gallery/src
.shots

# Build output — regenerated by buildCommand. Shipping a stale copy is worse
# than shipping none.
www/dist
.astro

# Repo-local tooling and prose; nothing in the build reads them.
docs
tests
.github
.remember
.superpowers
.playwright-mcp
*.log
.DS_Store
